<h1>edge connectivity</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
(1) The smallest number of <a href="edge.html"><em>edges</em></a> whose deletion will cause a <a href="connectedGraph.html"><em>connected graph</em></a> to not be connected.  (2) For a pair of vertices s and t in a graph, the smallest number of edges whose deletion will separate s from t.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="vertexConnectivity.html"><em>vertex connectivity</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorGS">GS</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Steve Skiena's Stony Brook Algorithm Repository <a href="https://algorist.com/problems/Edge_and_Vertex_Connectivity.html" target="_blank">(C, C++, Java, and Mathematica)</a>

